# Written per run by `grade()` in src/run.ts, and never committed: their contents name the
# target of that run, and the internal shims carry an absolute path from whichever machine
# produced them. `vendored-suite.test.ts` asserts every path listed here is really ignored —
# four of them were committed once, with `/Users/…/burgee-wave3/…` inside.
vendor/*/shim*.js
vendor/*/shim*.mjs
vendor/*/vitest.config.mjs
vendor/*/vitest.setup.mjs
# The generated internal shims, at whatever path a host files its own modules: `lib/` for
# commander, dotenv and yargs, `src/` for cli-table3 and cosmiconfig, `build/` where a host
# compiles first.
#
# `src/` is named per host and the other two are not, because a host's *tests* can live
# there too: `lilconfig` files its suite at `src/spec/`, so the blanket `vendor/*/src/` this
# line replaced would have gitignored that whole vendored suite — never committed, and on CI
# "not vendored" instead of a rate. A missing rule is the loud failure (`vendored-suite.test.ts`
# computes each host's generated paths from its own `.source.json` and goes red for one it
# cannot match), so a third host filing internals under `src/` adds a line here and knows why.
vendor/*/lib/
vendor/cli-table3/src/
vendor/cosmiconfig/src/
vendor/*/build/
# Written by a *suite* rather than by the oracle, and upstream ignores both in its own
# repository (`node-cross-spawn/.gitignore`: `test/fixtures/(*` and `test/tmp/`). Its
# "special shell chars" case copies a fixture to a name made of them and never removes it,
# and its `beforeAll` makes `test/tmp`. Without these, running the suite dirties the
# worktree with two files whose names are `()%!^&;, ` and `()%!^&;, .bat` — which reads,
# to the next person, like something the vendor step produced.
vendor/cross-spawn/test/fixtures/(*
vendor/*/test/tmp/
results.json
results.control.json
upstream.json
vendor-diff.md
# A monorepo suite's own dependencies — `suiteDeps` in hosts.ts, installed into the
# vendored directory on the first grade and never into this workspace's manifest or
# lockfile. `@inquirer/testing`, `@clack/core`, and the incumbent itself for the control.
vendor/*/node_modules/
vendor/*/package-lock.json
# clack's internal shims: its tests sit in `packages/prompts/test/`, so `../src/common.js`
# is written under the sub-package, not at the vendored root like every host before it.
vendor/*/packages/prompts/src/
# The same two generated files for a monorepo host, where vitest's root is the
# sub-package's own directory rather than the vendored root.
vendor/*/packages/*/vitest.config.mjs
vendor/*/packages/*/vitest.setup.mjs
